@Test @TC6
Scenario: Validate borrower limit for a facility with an allocated borrower
  When user clicks on the edit icon for the "Facility 4" with an allocated borrower
  Then user clicks on overview tab and scrolls down to Facility Global Amount having value "$1000000"
  When User enters invalid amount "$1500000" into the limit field
  Then The value "$1500000" is displayed in the input field
  When User moves focus away from the limit field
  Then A validation error message is displayed
  When User corrects the limit to "$900000"
  And User clicks on save button
  Then The validation error message disappears

@Test @TC9
Scenario: Navigate to a deal with defined primary borrower
  When User navigates to a deal with defined primary borrower
  Then Deal Primary Borrower becomes "DealPrime" and Deal Additional Borrower becomes "DealSecond"
  And The deal overview page correctly shows "DealPrime" as the primary borrower for the entire deal
  When User selects "Facility J" and allocates both borrowers
  Then "DealPrime" is the default primary borrower for "Facility J"
  When User changes the primary borrower for "Facility J" to "DealSecond"
  Then The new facility primary borrower becomes "DealSecond"
  And On "Facility J" screen, "DealSecond" is shown as the primary borrower
  When User saves the facility changes
  Then The changes are saved successfully
  When User navigates back to the main deal overview page
  Then The deal overview page shows "DealPrime" as the primary borrower for the deal
  And The changes made at the facility level have not propagated to the deal level

@Test @TC10
Scenario: Navigate to deal with one borrower and two facilities
  When User navigates to deal with one borrower and two facilities
  Then Borrower becomes "Universal Borrower" with Facilities "Facility X" having amount "$500k" and "Facility Y" having amount "$2M"
  And The deal page is loaded
  When User selects "Facility X" and allocates it as "Universal Borrower"
  Then "Universal Borrower" is successfully allocated to "Facility X"
  When User sets the limit for "Universal Borrower" for "Facility X" as "$300000"
  Then The limit is set to "$300000" for "Universal Borrower" in "Facility X"
  And Changes are saved
  When User navigates to "Facility Y"
  Then The "Facility Y" details are displayed and "Universal Borrower" is not yet allocated
  When User allocates "Universal Borrower" to "Facility Y"
  Then "Universal Borrower" is successfully allocated to "Facility Y"
  And The limit field for "Universal Borrower" in "Facility Y" is empty or zero
  When User sets the limit as "$1000000" for "Universal Borrower" in "Facility Y"
  Then The limit is set to "$1000000" for "Universal Borrower" in "Facility Y"
  And Changes are saved
  When User navigates back to "Facility X"
  Then The view for "Facility X" is displayed
  And The limit for "Universal Borrower" is shown as "$300000"

@Test @TC11
Scenario: Navigate to facility with several allocated borrowers
  When User navigates to a facility with several allocated borrowers
  Then The facility shows 4 borrower tags
  And The allocated borrower count is "4"
  When User clicks "Select" to select borrowers
  Then 2 borrowers are selected
  And Both borrowers are highlighted or checked indicating they are selected
  When User selects two borrowers, the "Delete" button becomes active
  And User clicks the "Delete" button
  Then A confirmation prompt may appear
  When User confirms the deletion
  Then The two selected borrowers are removed from the facility
  And Tags for remaining 2 borrowers are still visible
  And The allocated borrower count updates from "4" to "2"  